Subject: [PATCH] fix: correct design.md->plan.md over-reach (CodeRabbit #297)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The blanket rename inverted legacy/backward-compat references. Fixes:
- lib/orientation.js: the `active_work_legacy_design` section reads `design.md`
  (the legacy fallback), not plan.md — restores the historical work-folder fallback.
- Revert docs/work/2026-06-06-kernel-backlog-memory-roadmap/ to master: those docs
  DISCUSS the design.md->plan.md migration ("legacy design.md", "design.md -> plan.md"),
  so blanket-replacing design.md->plan.md there produced nonsense ("plan.md -> plan.md",
  "legacy plan.md"). That folder already used plan.md as its own filename on master; only
  its migration-discussion content was corrupted, now restored.

Principle: rename current work-folder artifacts to plan.md, but preserve design.md wherever
it names the LEGACY/backward-compatible file or DISCUSSES the migration.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
